<article class="env-lemma" id="0FHB">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FHB">Lemma <span data-tag="0FHB">45.9.1</span>.</a> Assume given (D0), (D1), and (D3) satisfying (A). For $f : X \to Y$ a morphism of nonempty equidimensional smooth projective schemes over $k$ we have $f_*(f^*b \cup a) = b \cup f_*a$. If $g : Y \to Z$ is a second morphism with $Z$ nonempty smooth projective and equidimensional, then $g_* \circ f_* = (g \circ f)_*$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The first equality holds because 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \int _ Y c \cup b \cup f_*a = \int _ X f^*c \cup f^*b \cup a = \int _ Y c \cup f_*(f^*b \cup a).  \]
</div>
    <p>
       The second equality holds because 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \int _ Z c \cup (g \circ f)_*a = \int _ X (g \circ f)^*c \cup a = \int _ X f^* g^* c \cup a = \int _ Y g^*c \cup f_*a = \int _ Z c \cup g_*f_*a  \]
</div>
    <p>
       This ends the proof. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>